Z||000002||Cozmo||06-07-2001||09:17 AM||||Fieros have about bottomed out, price-wise.  It's worth getting them for a couple of hundred, even if only for parts.  It helps to have a place to store them, but at that price you can't go wrong.  Go for it!<BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||06-07-2001||09:29 AM||||Is it blue? If it is get it regardless of problems! Just look the car over very objectivly, ask questions about the car <BR>How long has he had it, where did he get it, how did he like that car, what work did he do on it, <BR>Turn on the headlights and see if the motors work, while there up and the hood is open look down inside the light well and bent metal down there?  if it has A/C does it work? does the fan come on when you kick on the A/C? (fan should operate even if the A/C doesn't) Look at the tires are the inflated right, have any cracks in them, look at the tread wear patterns, none, scalloped, ridges? you can tell a lot just by looking at the tires. <BR>Fire it up and let it run while you look at it and are asking questions. any fluid leaks? temp ok? any knocking going on? Oil pressure ok when warmed up? hit the horn a few times. <BR>Pop both hood and trunk deck while its running. Spare tire jack and lug wrench there? fluid bottles have fluid in them?<BR>Smell the exhaust (that should get a funny look out of him) smell oily?  sweet? or does it burn your nose and eyes. or is it just kinda bland propane(good) smelling. <BR>Look at the brakes thru the wheels see any ridges in the disk? while down there any wheel wells busted? rockers ok? chin spoiler ok? look at the jack points! and the coolant lines just behind them. Is everything ok no bends anywhere or kinked lines. Doors open and close right? look at the spaces between the panels any gaps bigger than the opposite side? any deep skuff marks on the threshholds? Operate the windows and mirrors.<P>Best thing you could ever do is get a mental picture of how your going to look things over and the questions you want to ask. The first thing I do is fire up the car then as it's running I do my inspection and ask questions. when I'm done I shut the car off then restart it again.<P>In the case of my Indy I just got the car without a serious inspection because it's gonna be a resto and not a daily driver / primay car.<P>Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||06-07-2001||09:45 AM||||take a torx 15 with you, pull the cover off the cigarette light panel, put a bent paper clip in the lower right two holes on the passenger side of the test connector, then turn the key to run, and dump the engine codes.<P>  it should blink once twice, once twice, once twice - those are normal, if it puts out any other ones (other that 1-2) then write them down and check the online service manual to see what the error codes are telling you.<P> get the VIN # and post it - someone must still have carfax here.||||reg||1
